NAME
	scan - network port and service detection module.

DESCRIPTION
	Perform network port scanning against a validated target. The module
	identifies open TCP ports and service banners using nmap. If nmap is
	not installed or unavailable in PATH, it seamlessly falls back to a
	pure-Python multi-threaded TCP socket port scanner for standard common ports.

UNDERLYING TOOL
	nmap (with native Python socket fallback)

EXECUTION
	nmap -sT -Pn -F <target>
	(Fallback: native Python socket connect across common ports)

USAGE
	use scan

MODULE OPTION
	target - target domain or IP.

COMMANDS
	show modules
		Display available modules.

	set target <domain/ip>
		Define the target domain or IP address.

	run
		Execute the port scanning module.

EXAMPLE
	use scan
	set target 127.0.0.1
	run

OUTPUT
	Structured list of open ports, protocol, service names, and
	persisted database records in SQLite.

REQUIREMENTS
	nmap (optional, recommended); built-in socket scanner used as fallback.

